# Build context for the api/worker image (context: ./core).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: without it the context was 63 MB and included .mypy_cache,
# .pytest_cache, .ruff_cache and every __pycache__ — directories that change on EVERY
# local lint or test run. That busted the `COPY . .` layer constantly, so an image
# rebuild happened when nothing shippable had changed, and the offline bundle
# (deploy/bundle.ps1) got a new 650 MB images.tar for no reason.
#
# WHAT MUST NOT BE EXCLUDED: `tests/` and `alembic/` stay in the image on purpose.
# `make gates` runs the full CI-identical suite INSIDE this image (ADR-006, Docker-only)
# and `alembic upgrade head` runs from the api container — excluding either would break
# testing and migrations, which is a far worse trade than a slightly larger context.

# Python bytecode and tool caches — regenerated, never shipped.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Coverage artifacts — written by `make gates` on the host bind-mount.
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# A host virtualenv must never reach the image: ADR-006 says there is no host Python,
# and copying one in would shadow the container's site-packages.
.venv/
venv/

# Editor/OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.swp
